{"text": "Lilly’s net margin did expand over the last twelve quarters, from 21.2% [f_62c800f1de18@2023-06-30] to 37.4% [f_62c800f1de18@2026-03-31], but the desk could not compute Lilly’s gross margin or operating margin because “LLY reports no gross_profit with a period; it may report a related line instead — call describe” and “LLY reports no operating_income with a period; it may report a related line instead — call describe.” So I cannot yet separate the expansion cleanly into pricing, mix, or cost from the computed margins alone. [table: net_margin_lly]

On Item 7, the filing says revenue in 2025 was 65,179 [f_c03f4ec9b7c7] and that “Revenue increased in 2025 driven primarily by increased volume, partially offset by lower realized prices.” It also says “Net income and earnings per share increased in 2025, primarily due to higher gross margin, partially offset by increased marketing, selling, and administrative expenses and research and development expenses.” That points to both pricing and mix/volume effects at the top line, with cost/investment pressure below gross profit limiting some of the operating leverage. The filing does not give a clean attribution of the margin expansion solely to one bucket in the quoted section. [f_c03f4ec9b7c7]

Merck is now being prepared, but it is not yet ready for the same margin comparison. The desk started readiness for MRK, and for now it returned “section_not_found” for Item 7 and could not derive gross, operating, or net margin for MRK. So at this stage I can only say that a like-for-like comparison against Merck is not available yet, not that Lilly is definitively better or worse on gross, operating, or net margin versus Merck."}

