{"text": "The latest run does not fully let me “reconcile factor contributions plus alpha and residual to the portfolio return” in the strict sense, because the desk returned the totals, not a factor-by-factor list. What it does show is that the reconciliation is incomplete on the figures shown: portfolio.reconcile.sum_of_position_contributions was 0.38% [f_8b862be47a4d], portfolio.reconcile.sum_of_factor_contributions was -0.47% [f_4c63f89d9d91], and portfolio.reconcile.alpha_plus_residual was 0.85% [f_d4578cf7ef52]. Those pieces sum to 0.76% on the figures provided, so the gap is 0.24% relative to 1.00% implied by a full return bridge, but the desk did not return the portfolio return itself, so I cannot state that as a quoted figure.

On what the desk did return, the factor side is net negative at -0.47% [f_4c63f89d9d91], while alpha plus residual is positive at 0.85% [f_d4578cf7ef52], and the position contribution line is 0.38% [f_8b862be47a4d]. The largest contributing factor cannot be named from this evidence because no factor-by-factor contribution table was returned. The smallest contributing factor also cannot be named for the same reason.

On HYG, its own 30d window return was 3.17% [f_d34d1efd3d01]. That does not match the sign of a negative contribution, because the only HYG-related contribution figures returned were concentration and exposure diagnostics, not the HYG factor contribution itself. So the desk evidence is insufficient to say “yes” or “no” on HYG’s contribution sign; what we can say is that HYG’s own price move over the period was positive at 3.17% [f_d34d1efd3d01]."}

